      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1aacfae1c260a37b276c0141eabd403650" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::map&lt; std::string, <ref refid="namespacethemisdb_1_1replication_1acfeea6095f4a51e57317a8befe704cad" kindref="member">ConsistencyLevel</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::map&lt;std::string, ConsistencyLevel&gt; themisdb::replication::MultiRegionActiveActiveConfig::collection_consistency_overrides</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>collection_consistency_overrides</name>
        <qualifiedname>themisdb::replication::MultiRegionActiveActiveConfig::collection_consistency_overrides</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Per-collection consistency overrides.</para>
<para>When a collection is present in this map, the configured level takes precedence over the caller-supplied level for both reads and writes. Use this to enforce STRONG consistency for critical collections while keeping the global default at BOUNDED_STALENESS or EVENTUAL.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Configuring STRONG here for a non-leader region will cause all writes to that collection to be rejected unless the local region is the designated leader. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/replication/replication_manager.h" line="1979" column="14" bodyfile="include/replication/replication_manager.h" bodystart="1979" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1aab3b84bbe8a4b693f6f48c46dcf5e622" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>std::string</type>
        <definition>std::string themisdb::replication::MultiRegionActiveActiveConfig::leader_region_id</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>leader_region_id</name>
        <qualifiedname>themisdb::replication::MultiRegionActiveActiveConfig::leader_region_id</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Designated leader region for STRONG cross-region writes.</para>
<para>When non-empty, <computeroutput>write()</computeroutput> calls with effective consistency <computeroutput>STRONG</computeroutput> are rejected if <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1a089721391cea7de502232d75396e1d42" kindref="member">local_region_id</ref> != <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1aab3b84bbe8a4b693f6f48c46dcf5e622" kindref="member">leader_region_id</ref></computeroutput>. This prevents split-brain lost-update scenarios for critical data by funnelling all strongly-consistent writes through a single region.</para>
<para>Leave empty to allow STRONG writes on any region (legacy behaviour; provides no cross-region linearisability guarantee). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/replication/replication_manager.h" line="1992" column="17" bodyfile="include/replication/replication_manager.h" bodystart="1992" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1afcef3a9f0beb19c7e8621475d50b384c" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool themisdb::replication::MultiRegionActiveActiveConfig::split_brain_detection_enabled</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>split_brain_detection_enabled</name>
        <qualifiedname>themisdb::replication::MultiRegionActiveActiveConfig::split_brain_detection_enabled</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= false</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Enable split-brain detection.</para>
<para>When <computeroutput>true</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>isSplitBrain()</computeroutput> returns <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if all peer regions report unhealthy staleness, indicating a possible network partition. Callers may choose to reject STRONG writes or emit alerts in this state. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/replication/replication_manager.h" line="2001" column="10" bodyfile="include/replication/replication_manager.h" bodystart="2001" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Configuration for <ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_manager" kindref="compound">MultiRegionActiveActiveManager</ref>.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Consistency Guarantees</heading>
</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>STRONG</computeroutput> consistency is only guaranteed within a single region.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Cross-region writes are always eventual unless <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1aab3b84bbe8a4b693f6f48c46dcf5e622" kindref="member">leader_region_id</ref></computeroutput> is set and all STRONG writes are routed exclusively through the designated leader.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Vector-clock-based conflict resolution (LAST_WRITE_WINS, MERGE) may produce different outcomes across regions for concurrent writes; this is expected in Active/Active deployments.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>For SERIALIZABLE or STRONG guarantees on critical data, restrict writes to a single region. Cross-region <computeroutput>STRONG</computeroutput> writes are rejected unless <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1a089721391cea7de502232d75396e1d42" kindref="member">local_region_id</ref> == <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1_multi_region_active_active_config_1aab3b84bbe8a4b693f6f48c46dcf5e622" kindref="member">leader_region_id</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
